# Closed-loop Part 1: live forward-camera heading into EKF3 via ExternalNav YAW ONLY.
# Appended after closedloop.parm (AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3) by sim/tools/closed_loop_run.sh HEADING=1.
# Not for dataset flights. Sources (pinned 7bac20cbcc) in heading_bridge_core.py and METHODOLOGY.
#
# VISO_TYPE 1 = MAVLink pass-through (AP_VisualOdom_MAV). NOT 3 (VOXL): 3 selects the IntelT265
# driver (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:145-147), whose yaw trim and reset-jump handling target VIO, and whose
# automatic yaw alignment is refused when ExtNav is the yaw source (AP_VisualOdom_IntelT265.cpp:143-146).
VISO_TYPE 1
# ExternalNav yaw; POSXY stays 0 (None), VELXY 5 (flow), POSZ 2 (rangefinder)
EK3_SRC1_YAW 6
# quality = floor(50*support/S_MIN): VISO_QUAL_MIN 50 accepts exactly the frozen Phase 3 validity
VISO_QUAL_MIN 50
# Ruling 2026-09-29: the documented minimum. angErr (0.148 deg) is clamped up to 0.05 rad, then
# EKF3's hard 5 deg floor applies (AP_NavEKF3_Measurements.cpp:1118): effective sigma 5.00 deg.
VISO_YAW_M_NSE 0.05
# Ruling D2 2026-09-30: C++ heading node; VISO_DELAY_MS = round(min latency) by the original G4 rule
# (gt_heading_cpp: 37.9 ms VISP, 40.0 ms node). Was 60 for the Python node (ruling 2026-09-29, G4 stop -> option 1:
# largest value inside the 60 ms horizon; Python min latency 100-104 ms). See METHODOLOGY.
VISO_DELAY_MS 38
